sunxi: use the MMC environment driver when booted over FEL

env_get_location() has no environment location for BOOT_DEVICE_BOARD
(FEL boot) unless ENV_IS_IN_FAT, ENV_IS_IN_UBI or ENV_IS_NOWHERE is
enabled. With only ENV_IS_IN_MMC, env_init() finds no driver at
priority 0 and returns -ENODEV, and the pre-relocation init sequence
stops before the console exists.

Return ENVL_MMC for FEL boots. When no card is present the load fails
into the default environment, which is the right behavior for a
RAM-loaded U-Boot.

--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -167,6 +167,8 @@
 			return ENVL_FAT;
 		break;
 	case BOOT_DEVICE_BOARD:
+		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_MMC))
+			return ENVL_MMC;
 		break;
 	default:
 		break;

